==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|rēctō}} {{m|la|folium|foliō|on the right leaf, on the right page}}, the [[Appendix:Glossary#ablative case|ablative case]] of the Latin {{m|la|rēctus||right}}. Compare {{m|la|versus||turned}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛk.toʊ/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Recto and verso}}
{{en-noun}}

# The front side of a flat object which is to be examined visually, as for reading, such as a sheet, leaf, [[coin]] or [[medal]].
# {{lb|en|printing}} The [[right-hand]] [[page]] of a [[book]] of a script which reads from left to right, usually having an odd page number.
# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[writ]] of [[right]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|front side of a flat object}} {{l|en|front}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|front side of a flat object}} {{l|en|verso}}, {{l|en|flipside}}
* {{sense|right-hand page of a book}} {{l|en|reverso}}

